<section class="thermal-section" aria-labelledby="thermal-title">
  <div class="thermal-inner">
    <figure class="thermal-visual" style="--split: 65%">
      <div class="wall-view" role="img" aria-label="A plain interior wall, as seen by the eye">
        <span class="wall-caption">WALL AS YOU SEE IT</span>
      </div>
      <div class="heat-view" role="img" aria-label="Thermal camera view revealing a warm water line leaking behind the wall">
        <span class="heat-caption">THERMAL VIEW: WARM WATER LINE LEAKING</span>
      </div>
      <span class="heat-reading">IR · 98.4°F hotspot</span>
      <span class="slider-divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <input class="thermal-slider" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="65" aria-label="Compare the normal wall with its thermal image" aria-valuetext="65% thermal view" />
    </figure>

    <div class="thermal-copy">
      <p class="thermal-kicker">Thermal imaging</p>
      <h2 id="thermal-title">See the Leak Before You Open the Wall</h2>
      <p>Water changes the temperature of whatever it touches. A leaking hot-water line warms the slab or drywall around it; a cold line cools it. Our thermal imaging cameras read those differences across a whole room in seconds, so we can trace a supply line through a wall or floor and spot where the pattern breaks.</p>
      <p>Thermal imaging narrows the search. Acoustic listening then confirms it. The combination is what lets our techs find leaks that other companies cannot.</p>
      <ul class="thermal-benefits">
        <li><span class="heat-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><strong>Thermal imaging cameras</strong> spot heat signatures from hot or cold water leaks behind walls and under floors.</span></li>
        <li><span class="heat-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><strong>Electronic amplifiers &amp; ground microphones</strong> hear buried supply lines through soil, asphalt, and concrete.</span></li>
        <li><span class="heat-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><strong>Tracer gas</strong> for situations where acoustic detection alone is not enough.</span></li>
        <li><span class="heat-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><strong>Pressure testing</strong> confirms which line is losing water.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  const thermalSection = document.querySelector('.thermal-section');
  const thermalVisual = thermalSection?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.thermal-visual');
  const thermalSlider = thermalSection?.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('.thermal-slider');
  if (thermalVisual && thermalSlider) {
    thermalSlider.addEventListener('input', () => {
      thermalVisual.style.setProperty('--split', `${thermalSlider.value}%`);
      thermalSlider.setAttribute('aria-valuetext', `${thermalSlider.value}% thermal view`);
    });
  }
</script>

